Laws from e-Gov and the eCFR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In koyomi and yuen, and so in `ritsu` and `ritsu.wasm`.

`koyomi explain` and `yuen explain` give, for each code, the smallest input that makes it, and
some of those inputs read an article of a law. For them, the ledgers of the two languages
(src/codes.rs of each) hold these copies, as the repository keeps them:

  crates/koyomi/examples/sources/law/129AC0000000089@2026-10-01/MainProvision-Article_142.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/fixtures/period/sources/law/129AC0000000089@2026-10-01/MainProvision-Article_142.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/mutants/E107_同じ条の違う本文/cal/sources/law/129AC0000000089@2026-10-01/MainProvision-Article_142.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/mutants/E107_同じ条の違う本文/sources/law/129AC0000000089@2026-10-01/MainProvision-Article_142.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/fixtures/period_of_months/sources/law/37-CFR-1@2026-01-01/1.7.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/mutants/E107_same_article_different_text/rules/sources/law/29-CFR-1910@2026-01-01/1910.157.xml
  crates/yuen/tests/mutants/E107_same_article_different_text/sources/law/29-CFR-1910@2026-01-01/1910.157.xml

The first four are Article 142 of the Civil Code of Japan (民法, 明治二十九年法律第八十九号, law ID
`129AC0000000089`) as of 2026-10-01, revision `129AC0000000089_20260624_508AC0000000045`, as
e-Gov's law API, version 2, served it on 2026-10-02. The terms of use of the e-Gov Law Search
(e-Gov 法令検索 利用規約, <https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/terms/>) put its content under the Public Data
License, version 1.0 (公共データ利用規約（第1.0版）, PDL1.0,
<https://www.digital.go.jp/resources/open_data/public_data_license_v1.0>), and ask that the
source be given, in the form of their examples:

出典：e-Gov法令検索（https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/）の「民法」（明治二十九年法律第八十九号）第百四十二条（2026年10月1日時点、版 129AC0000000089_20260624_508AC0000000045）、法令API Version2 で2026年10月2日に取得、PDL1.0

They also ask that content which was edited say so, apart from the source, and that it not be
presented as if the government had made it. The fourth copy is edited: it changes 翌日 to 翌々日
in the article on purpose, so that yuen's E107 (one article with two texts) has an example. The
other three are as e-Gov served them.

The last three are 37 CFR 1.7 and 29 CFR 1910.157 as of 2026-01-01, as the eCFR's versioner API
served them. The Code of Federal Regulations is a work of the United States government and is
